{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d979592e-6e14-48a4-9a51-d55dae6a8e29","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad94e84a78e904c6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-ks66mr2k/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E001.md","content":"# Investigate workspace resolution initialization dependencies in the artifacts-only server context\n\n## Description\n\nResolves whether the workspace resolution provided by the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin — the `kubernetes-auth` workspace provider registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry` — can be initialized and exercised in an artifacts-only MLflow server where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. This is the strategy's flagged risk \"Auth plugin coupling to full server initialization\" and its open question \"Does the workspace store initialization in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins depend on tracking store availability?\". The outcome determines the scope of plugin refactoring needed for the artifacts-only context and the feasibility of initializing only the workspace provider in the artifacts-only server.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Map the initialization path of the Kubernetes workspace store (`kubernetes://` URI scheme) and the plugin's workspace resolution: what each step imports, what it requires, and whether any step depends on tracking store or model registry store availability.\n- Determine whether experiment-to-workspace resolution can be exercised in a server context with no tracking or model registry stores initialized.\n- If the resolution is coupled to the full server initialization path: identify the concrete refactoring needed to factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, and assess its size.\n- Deliver the findings as a documented determination with code-level evidence and a refactoring scope assessment usable for planning the plugin and server implementation work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written determination, with code-level references, of whether workspace store initialization in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins depends on tracking store availability — a definitive yes/no answering the strategy's open question.\n- If coupled: a refactoring plan identifying what must move to an independent initialization path, with the affected surfaces enumerated.\n- If not coupled: verification evidence (for example, a runnable reproduction) that workspace resolution works without tracking or model registry store initialization.\n- A recommendation, stated in pass/fail terms usable for scheduling, on whether the plugin requires extension or only verification for the artifacts-only context.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Enables HLR-2 (P0, workspace-membership validation of artifact requests) and HLR-7 (P1, plugin workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context) by resolving the unknown that determines their implementation scope.\n- Derives from the strategy's risk \"Auth plugin coupling to full server initialization\" and its dependency note on the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":80362,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1d420f326264026","agent_id":"a42a760e8aa834b42","session_id":"17a14eab-664e-4874-b0eb-335a5501da93","uuid":"d40cff03-2de7-461c-8342-b6b74537c5af","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:27:34.997Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
