{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d979592e-6e14-48a4-9a51-d55dae6a8e29","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a441ca5f0f61998c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-ks66mr2k/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E003.md","content":"# Investigate artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n\n## Description\n\nResolves how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to a dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology. This is the strategy's open question \"How should the operator configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking server to the dedicated artifacts-only instance?\" — the answer affects the HTTPRoute design and determines whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations. The outcome determines the routing approach implemented in the operator's split-server topology work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Evaluate routing options for directing artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment's ingress to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, within the operator's existing Gateway API HTTPRoute pattern (HTTPRoutes are created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery).\n- Determine whether the main tracking server needs a configuration change — or a code change — to delegate artifact operations to the dedicated instance, and identify the specific configuration surface if so.\n- Produce a design decision with rationale and trade-offs that the split-topology operator implementation can build against, covering the HTTPRoute structure and any tracking-deployment configuration.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A documented routing design describing how artifact traffic is routed from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, consistent with the operator's conditional Gateway API HTTPRoute pattern.\n- A definitive determination of whether the tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations, with the configuration surface identified if yes.\n- The design decision recorded with rationale and trade-offs, in a form the split-topology operator implementation can directly apply.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Enables HLR-5 and HLR-6 (P1, dedicated artifacts-only instance deployment and artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment) by selecting the routing approach.\n- Derives from the strategy's open question on artifact traffic routing configuration (owner: MLflow Team).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":80362,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1d420f326264026","agent_id":"a42a760e8aa834b42","session_id":"17a14eab-664e-4874-b0eb-335a5501da93","uuid":"d73d288f-1c8e-4239-aba5-68b15118f5d4","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:27:44.308Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
