{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-618e5bc9-f0d2-4570-a9a1-d2f0957ec262","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3311028c0107b9a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-ks66mr2k/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E005.md","content":"# Artifacts-only workspace resolution in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\n\n## Description\n\nMakes the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin's workspace resolution function correctly in the artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The plugin already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking server's non-artifact operations, registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`; this epic verifies that resolution in the artifacts-only context and extends it where it is currently coupled to the full tracking server initialization path. Workspace authorization reuses the existing auth plugin infrastructure — the strategy deliberately does not dictate Kubernetes API authorization mechanics. The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup are unchanged: authentication at the ingress level works identically for the tracking server and the artifacts-only instance.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Verify the plugin's workspace resolution in a server context with no tracking or model registry stores initialized, per the documented findings on its initialization dependencies.\n- Where resolution is coupled to the full server initialization path, factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin.\n- Preserve the existing integration surface: registration through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loading via `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`, so the tracking server and the artifacts-only server load the same plugin.\n- Maintain the tracking server's existing workspace resolution behavior for non-artifact operations (no regression).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The plugin's workspace resolution correctly resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping in a server context where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized.\n- The workspace resolution used by the tracking server's non-artifact operations is unchanged, verified by the plugin's existing test suite.\n- The plugin loads through the existing entry point and registry mechanism, with no new registration surface introduced.\n- If refactoring was required: the independent initialization path is covered by tests demonstrating workspace resolution without tracking store availability.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization. (Raised to P0 by priority inheritance: this capability enables the P0 workspace-membership validation of artifact requests, HLR-2.)\n- Enables HLR-2 (P0): the server's per-request workspace validation delegates to this resolution capability.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":82497,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1d420f326264026","agent_id":"a42a760e8aa834b42","session_id":"17a14eab-664e-4874-b0eb-335a5501da93","uuid":"5329d7fc-8dc9-40cf-b740-82a145690a83","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:28:03.269Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
