{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-973b3da882365a57","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n3\ttitle: Investigate artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 0\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to a dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology. This is the strategy's open question \"How should the operator configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking server to the dedicated artifacts-only instance?\" — the answer affects the HTTPRoute design and determines whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations. The outcome determines the routing approach implemented in the operator's split-server topology work.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Evaluate routing options for directing artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment's ingress to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, within the operator's existing Gateway API HTTPRoute pattern (HTTPRoutes are created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery).\n34\t- Determine whether the main tracking server needs a configuration change — or a code change — to delegate artifact operations to the dedicated instance, and identify the specific configuration surface if so.\n35\t- Produce a design decision with rationale and trade-offs that the split-topology operator implementation can build against, covering the HTTPRoute structure and any tracking-deployment configuration.\n36\t\n37\t## Acceptance Criteria\n38\t\n39\t- A documented routing design describing how artifact traffic is routed from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, consistent with the operator's conditional Gateway API HTTPRoute pattern.\n40\t- A definitive determination of whether the tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations, with the configuration surface identified if yes.\n41\t- The design decision recorded with rationale and trade-offs, in a form the split-topology operator implementation can directly apply.\n42\t\n43\t## HLR Traceability\n44\t\n45\t- Enables HLR-5 and HLR-6 (P1, dedicated artifacts-only instance deployment and artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment) by selecting the routing approach.\n46\t- Derives from the strategy's open question on artifact traffic routing configuration (owner: MLflow Team).\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-857b1162f4264d94","agent_id":"a733d258d89a3b029","session_id":"17a14eab-664e-4874-b0eb-335a5501da93","uuid":"4eea3d67-5ca0-4c4a-8e3a-f9ef8afe6e73","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:30:51.509Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-973b3da882365a57","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
