{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0a206ec8e8285c9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: Artifacts-only workspace resolution in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If workspace store initialization is already decoupled from tracking\n15\t    store availability, reduce scope to verification and regression coverage; if the\n16\t    coupling is deeper than an independent initialization path can address, re-plan\n17\t    the workspace resolution approach for the artifacts-only context before implementing.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 0\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Artifacts-only workspace resolution in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tMakes the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin's workspace resolution function correctly in the artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The plugin already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking server's non-artifact operations, registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`; this epic verifies that resolution in the artifacts-only context and extends it where it is currently coupled to the full tracking server initialization path. Workspace authorization reuses the existing auth plugin infrastructure — the strategy deliberately does not dictate Kubernetes API authorization mechanics. The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup are unchanged: authentication at the ingress level works identically for the tracking server and the artifacts-only instance.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Verify the plugin's workspace resolution in a server context with no tracking or model registry stores initialized, per the documented findings on its initialization dependencies.\n44\t- Where resolution is coupled to the full server initialization path, factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin.\n45\t- Preserve the existing integration surface: registration through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loading via `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`, so the tracking server and the artifacts-only server load the same plugin.\n46\t- Maintain the tracking server's existing workspace resolution behavior for non-artifact operations (no regression).\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- The plugin's workspace resolution correctly resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping in a server context where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized.\n51\t- The workspace resolution used by the tracking server's non-artifact operations is unchanged, verified by the plugin's existing test suite.\n52\t- The plugin loads through the existing entry point and registry mechanism, with no new registration surface introduced.\n53\t- If refactoring was required: the independent initialization path is covered by tests demonstrating workspace resolution without tracking store availability.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization. (Raised to P0 by priority inheritance: this capability enables the P0 workspace-membership validation of artifact requests, HLR-2.)\n58\t- Enables HLR-2 (P0): the server's per-request workspace validation delegates to this resolution capability.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-857b1162f4264d94","agent_id":"a733d258d89a3b029","session_id":"17a14eab-664e-4874-b0eb-335a5501da93","uuid":"f9740e8e-c4d9-496e-98fe-40bff9e19b49","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:30:55.234Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0a206ec8e8285c9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
