{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8e1e1fc04581c9a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n3\ttitle: Split-server artifacts-only topology in the MLflow operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the routing design requires a different HTTPRoute topology\n15\t    or tracking-server code changes, update the split-deployment configuration approach\n16\t    and re-plan the routing portion of the operator work before implementing.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 5\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Split-server artifacts-only topology in the MLflow operator\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tExtends the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, and to configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to that dedicated instance — a split-server topology, not a single-deployment configuration toggle (per Staff Engineer / SME input). The main tracking server continues to handle experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry; the artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace validation. The operator uses its existing Helm-in-operator pattern — the MLflow CR spec is converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, and applied via Server-Side Apply — and propagates workspace configuration to the artifacts-only instance using the same mechanisms it uses for the main tracking deployment. Gateway API HTTPRoute resources are created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute, separate from the main tracking Deployment's resources.\n43\t- Configuration of the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, per the routing design selected under this strategy.\n44\t- Propagation of workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the operator's existing configuration mechanisms, so the artifacts-only Deployment runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`.\n45\t- Operator validation that rejects MLflow CR configurations where the artifacts-only instance would be deployed without the workspace flags, so misconfiguration cannot result in artifact requests bypassing workspace validation.\n46\t- kube-rbac-proxy sidecar deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, reconciliation creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment, measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n51\t- The artifacts-only Deployment's container command includes `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`, measured by inspecting the rendered Deployment spec.\n52\t- The main tracking deployment is configured to route artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the selected routing design, and artifact requests through the main tracking deployment's route reach the dedicated instance.\n53\t- The operator rejects, with a clear status condition, MLflow CR configurations that enable the artifacts-only instance without the workspace flags.\n54\t- HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance are created only when the Gateway API CRD is present at runtime, consistent with the operator's conditional CRD discovery pattern.\n55\t- The rendered split topology is idempotent under repeated reconciliation (server-side apply produces no spurious changes).\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-5 (P1): the MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n60\t- HLR-6 (P1): the main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-857b1162f4264d94","agent_id":"a733d258d89a3b029","session_id":"17a14eab-664e-4874-b0eb-335a5501da93","uuid":"fe13d9cb-b29d-468a-b94e-0ae224395c04","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:30:55.811Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8e1e1fc04581c9a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
